Uploaded avatars are written here, at runtime, under images/avatars/.

The directory is committed (via this file) rather than created on first upload
for two reasons:

  * The SDK's static-web-assets manifest, loaded at startup in Development,
    resolves paths under wwwroot. If the folder is missing, the app throws
    before it can serve anything.
  * UseStaticFiles builds its file provider once, at startup. A directory that
    only appears later is invisible to it, so those files 404 forever.

Uploaded files themselves are NOT committed. Add images/avatars/ to
.gitignore if this is ever committed from a machine that has uploaded.
